WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-21, with 0.0.2


STATE

  Version 0.0.2, pipelines and redirections, on branch dev. It adds
  pipelines (`|`, `!`), and-or lists (`&&`, `||`) with multi-line
  continuation, all POSIX redirection operators (`<`, `>`, `>|`, `>>`,
  `<>`, `<&`, `>&` with IO numbers and `-` to close), here-documents
  (`<<`, `<<-` with quoted delimiter support and in-memory size cap),
  and descriptor save/restore around builtins. readelf -d lists only
  libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass: unit tests, script tests
  against bash --posix, and refusal tests.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; lint mode is P2 0.1.5; tam-clam ships only its own key
  map (no built-in readline map), drafted in arch/keys.md and agreed with
  Fred before 0.2.0.


NEXT

  1. 0.0.3, variables and parameter expansion (plans/P1-foundation.md):
     - variable table (src/var.c): shell variables, exported variables,
       read-only flags, imported from environ at start-up;
     - assignments before a command and assignment-only commands;
     - words as a list of parts (literal, quoted literal, parameter) in
       the parser instead of raw text;
     - POSIX parameter expansion, special parameters ($? $$ $! $# $@ $*
       $- $0), positional parameters, PS1/PS2, tilde expansion, and
       logical cd.
     Bump VERSION to 0.0.3 in the first code commit.

  2. 0.0.4, compound commands and functions (plans/P1-foundation.md).


